# Pilotbook

This is the Pilotbook source tree. Use `pnpm pb`, not `npx pilotbook`. Work items live as markdown with YAML frontmatter. Do not move files to change status.

Follow [skills/implement.md](skills/implement.md), [skills/architect.md](skills/architect.md), [skills/groom.md](skills/groom.md), [skills/prioritize.md](skills/prioritize.md), and [skills/discover.md](skills/discover.md).

1. `pnpm pb next` — pick unblocked work
2. `pnpm pb brief <ID>` — load governing rules, ADRs, and parent stories before editing code
3. Implement against the brief. Linked BR-/ADR- files win over improvisation.
4. `pnpm pb verify <ID>` then set `status: done`
5. `pnpm pb lint` must exit 0. `pnpm pb board` refreshes the generated board.

Create items with `pnpm pb new <type> --title "..."`. Never invent IDs.
